# No version or date-released: releases are cut automatically on every green
# push to main, so either field would be stale by the next commit.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: arena
abstract: >-
  Reusable batch storage for Go slices and strings, reducing allocation and GC
  scanning overhead with 12-byte pointer-free references. Values that share a
  lifetime are packed into reusable chunks and returned as ordinary Go views.
  Reset reuses storage for the next batch. Holding millions of strings as
  AppendStringRef descriptors and resolving them with StringValue as needed
  removes per-string pointer scanning and its CPU cost on each garbage
  collection cycle. Byte chunks and descriptor arrays contain no pointers;
  chunk headers and live string views still need scanning.
authors:
  - family-names: Lindvall
    given-names: Johan
repository-code: https://github.com/JohanLindvall/arena
url: https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/JohanLindvall/arena
license: MIT
keywords:
  - go
  - arena allocator
  - memory management
  - garbage collection
